# A3's boundary, asserted as today's fact.  `1 << 1000` is 1001 decimal digits
# under the V2 ruling (Z is arbitrary precision), and this engine cannot hold
# that number yet: the ruling's shape is "immediate plus a heap object on
# overflow" (docs/HANDOFF_INFIVERSE.md section 2.8) and it is not implemented.
# So TODAY this must be refused -- and this test asserts the refusal.  When the
# heap-object form lands, `shl(1, 1000)` will succeed, this test will go RED,
# and that red is the signal to replace it with A3's real form: 1001 digits.
say shl(1, 1000)
